---
title: Deterministic fake data
intent: Send seeded fake names and emails to a local echo endpoint.
group: core
features:
- faker
command: curlew run examples/cookbook/faker.yaml --var mud="$MUDFLAT_URL" --var ws="$MUDFLAT_WS_URL" --var run="$RUN_ID" --seed 42
order: 40
runnable: true
---

The seed controls generated values. It does not make network timings, run IDs or wall-clock timestamps reproducible. Inspect the request body in a verbose report to compare generated values.

## Prerequisites

Use the complete repository checkout and start Mudflat as described in the [cookbook setup](https://github.com/weiqigod/curlew/blob/main/site/README.md). Run these commands from the repository root with `curlew` on PATH.

```bash
export MUDFLAT_URL="${MUDFLAT_URL:-http://127.0.0.1:18080}"
export MUDFLAT_WS_URL="${MUDFLAT_WS_URL:-ws://127.0.0.1:18080}"
export RUN_ID="cookbook-$(date +%s)-$$"
```

## Run it

```bash
curlew run examples/cookbook/faker.yaml --var mud="$MUDFLAT_URL" --var ws="$MUDFLAT_WS_URL" --var run="$RUN_ID" --seed 42
```

A successful execution exits 0. Read assertion outcomes as well as the exit code.
No example output or timing numbers are fabricated here.

## Complete collection

<!-- cookbook-source: examples/cookbook/faker.yaml -->
```yaml
name: Deterministic payload
requests:
  - name: Echo generated name
    request:
      method: POST
      url: "{{mud}}/echo"
      body:
        name: "{{$faker.fullName}}"
        email: "{{$faker.email}}"
    assertions:
      status: 200
      body:
        $.request.body_len: { greater_than: 0 }
```
